## State Management Principles

- Separate ephemeral from app state
- Use built-in solutions first
- Avoid unnecessary third-party packages
- Keep state close to usage
- Minimize state mutations
- Make state predictable
- Follow @lib/features/shared/models/feature_state.dart patterns

## Equatable State Pattern

- Extend `Equatable` for all state classes
- Override `props` getter for comparisons
- Use `const` constructors for immutability
- Include all relevant fields in `props`
- Apply generic types for data states
- Handle null values in props properly
- Test state equality behavior

## Monica State Architecture

```dart
// Base state class with Equatable
abstract class FeatureState extends Equatable {
  const FeatureState();

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => <Object?>[];
}

// Specific state implementations
class LoadingState extends FeatureState {
  const LoadingState([this.message]);

  final String? message;

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => <Object?>[message];
}

class SuccessState<T> extends FeatureState {
  const SuccessState(this.data, [this.message]);

  final T data;
  final String? message;

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => <Object?>[data, message];
}
```

## Built-in Solutions

- Use `setState` for simple local state
- Apply `ValueNotifier` for single values
- Use `ChangeNotifier` for complex state
- Implement `InheritedWidget` for deep sharing
- Use `FutureBuilder` for async operations
- Apply `StreamBuilder` for streams
- Prefer `ListenableBuilder` over rebuilds

## State Organization

- Group state by feature
- Create immutable state models
- Use Equatable for comparisons
- Implement state factories
- Define clear state transitions
- Document state dependencies
- Follow Monica state patterns

## Common State Types

- `InitialState` for component initialization
- `LoadingState` with optional messages
- `SuccessState<T>` with typed data
- `ErrorState` with error details
- `EmptyState` for no-data scenarios
- Apply consistent naming conventions
- Use generic types when appropriate

## ValueNotifier Pattern

```dart
final ValueNotifier<int> counter = ValueNotifier<int>(0);

ValueListenableBuilder<int>(
  valueListenable: counter,
  builder: (context, value, child) {
    return Text('Count: $value');
  },
);
```

## Data Flow Architecture

- Implement repository pattern @lib/db/repositories/
- Use service interfaces @lib/services/interfaces/
- Abstract data sources
- Handle errors at service level
- Transform data in repositories
- Keep UI layer thin
- Apply dependency injection

## State Best Practices

- Initialize state in `initState()`
- Dispose resources in `dispose()`
- Avoid state in build methods
- Prevent unnecessary rebuilds
- Use `const` constructors everywhere
- Profile state performance
- Test state transitions thoroughly
- Use `super.key` in stateful widgets